TI  - Percutaneous Dilational Tracheostomy.
PG  - 211-222
LID - S0272-5231(17)30120-X [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.ccm.2017.11.009 [doi]
AB  - Tracheostomy tubes can be inserted surgically or percutaneously via percutaneous 
      dilational tracheostomy (PDT). Tracheostomy is performed for upper airway 
      obstruction, though more often to allow prolonged mechanical ventilation in place 
      of endotracheal tubes. Preparation, performance, and postoperative management for 
      PDT are best provided by a multidisciplinary team. Although PDT is a safe 
      procedure in the hands of experienced operators, both early and late 
      complications can arise. Caution must also be taken during early tracheostomy 
      tube exchange given that immaturity of the stomal tract can risk loss of the 
      airway.
