TI  - Comparison of surgical and percutaneous dilational tracheostomy.
PG  - 423-9
AB  - When significant clinical end points are considered, PDT is a cost-effective and 
      safe alternative to ST in critically ill patients in the ICU when performed by 
      skilled and experienced practitioners [1, 40]. There are insufficient data to 
      establish clear superiority of either technique. Important advantages of PDT may 
      include eliminating the need for operating room facilities and personnel by the 
      performance of the procedure at the bedside and significantly decreasing the time 
      interval between the decision to perform tracheostomy and the actual procedure 
      [1, 2, 20].
