DP  - 2016 Feb 15
TI  - Anesthetic Implications for Tracheal Injury During Bronchoscopy-Guided 
      Percutaneous Dilational Tracheostomy.
PG  - 90-4
LID - 10.1213/XAA.0000000000000291 [doi]
AB  - Bronchoscopic-guided percutaneous dilational tracheostomy has become one of the 
      most common elective tracheostomy methods for patients requiring prolonged 
      ventilatory support. The safety profile, patient selection, and risks as well as 
      complication management, when compared with an open surgical technique, remain 
      somewhat controversial with no clear recommendations. We present a case of a 
      critically ill patient undergoing percutaneous dilation tracheostomy complicated 
      by tracheal wall injury and airway loss. The airway was successfully 
      conservatively managed as well as the tracheal injury. Anesthetic implications, 
      safety, and management options as well as recommendations are reviewed.
