TI  - Percutaneous Dilational Tracheostomy in a Patient With SARS-CoV-2 (COVID-19) 
      Disease: A Case Report With Implications in Staff Safety.
PG  - e13769
LID - 10.7759/cureus.13769 [doi]
LID - e13769
AB  - Some patients may need mechanical ventilation support during severe acute 
      respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2) (coronavirus disease-2019, 
      COVID-19) infection and may eventually require tracheostomy in the following 
      days. Tracheostomy is considered as a high-risk procedure for surgeons and 
      operative personnel in terms of air contamination. We present a case of 
      percutaneous dilational tracheostomy performed in a patient with COVID-19 
      pneumonia and the methods we used to reduce contamination risks for the 
      healthcare staff.
