VI  - 13
IP  - 2
DP  - 2009 Apr-Jun
TI  - Airway bleed after percutaneous tracheostomy is not always procedure-related.
PG  - 96-8
LID - 10.4103/0972-5229.56057 [doi]
AB  - Tracheotomies are the most frequent surgical procedures performed in the 
      intensive care unit. We present a case of major hemorrhage that occurred in the 
      intensive care unit during an elective percutaneous dilational tracheostomy in a 
      46-year-old female diagnosed with multiple myeloma. The patient was later taken 
      to the operation theatre and procedure-related cause of bleeding was ruled out. 
      It was subsequently realized that the cause of bleeding was intrapulmonary and 
      occurred coincidently with the tracheostomy.
