      bleeding after percutaneous dilational tracheostomy.
PG  - 665-667
LID - 10.1002/ccr3.2061 [doi]
AB  - In our case, the use of a low intravenous bolus dose of rFVIIa (recombinant 
      factor VII activated; 15-20 mcg/kg) was effective and uneventful in controlling 
      late postprocedural PDT bleeding associated with thrombocytopenia that cannot be 
      corrected and after all other treatments failed.
