DP  - 2002 Jun
TI  - Enlargement of existing tracheostome using percutaneous dilators.
PG  - 451-3
AB  - Children requiring long-term mechanical ventilation or with abnormalities of the 
      upper airway may need a tracheostomy for prolonged periods of time. For these 
      children, insertion of a larger tracheostomy tube may be required to match 
      somatic growth. We describe a new method of enlarging the tracheal stoma in 
      children, based on the existing technique of percutaneous dilational 
      tracheostomy.
